---
code: wrapper-peel-incoherent
when-fires: a wrapper's `__predict` and `__lend_map` disagree on the peel tail position. oracle/validate.rs peel_and_entry_coherence. Spanned (the predict name_span).
why: 273 §5 (declarations-genuinely-contradict): a pre-network fail-fast. The holes are typed: `{wrapper}` plus the two disagreeing depths.
---
-- book.sh --
#!/bin/sh
sudo hork add nginx

-- sudo.oracle.sh --
# dorc-lang/v0.2
sudo__predict() { shift; "$@"; }
sudo__lend_map() { : lends user; : lends fs-view; : lends netns; "$@"; }

-- replay --
$ dorc plan --book=book.sh --pre-source sudo.oracle.sh > /dev/null
wrapper: error[wrapper-peel-incoherent]: Wrapper `sudo`'s `__predict` and
`__lend_map` disagree on where the guest begins: `__predict` reaches `"$@"`
after 1 argv token(s), `__lend_map` after 0, so the guest would start at a
different token depending on which member dispatched, and Dorc stops before
contacting any host. Fix whichever argparse is wrong so both members peel to the
same tail.
